<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="How the Calendar Manager demo handles account, calendar and session information."><title>Privacy and cookies | Calendar Manager</title><style>body{font:16px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#172033;background:#f3f6fb;margin:0;padding:2rem}main{max-width:48rem;margin:auto;background:white;border-radius:16px;padding:2rem}h1,h2{line-height:1.25}a{color:#174dc4}</style></head><body><main><a href="index.php">← Back to demo</a><h1>Privacy and cookie notice</h1><p>Calendar Manager is a demonstration project by Aziz Kouki. Contact <a href="mailto:aziz@azizkouki.com">aziz@azizkouki.com</a> with privacy questions or requests.</p><h2>Information you provide</h2><p>When you register, the application stores your username, email address and a password hash. It also stores calendar entries, including their names, descriptions, start and end dates, and approval status or rejection reason. Administrators can review and manage accounts and requests. Please use fictional information and a unique password; do not enter sensitive or confidential information.</p><h2>How the information is used</h2><p>The application uses account information to authenticate users and calendar information to display and manage scheduling requests. Data is stored in a MySQL database. This demo is hosted on Render and uses an Aiven database; requests may also pass through the portfolio hosting infrastructure. These providers may process technical information such as IP addresses and server logs when delivering their services.</p><h2>Cookies and external resources</h2><p>A necessary PHP session cookie keeps your demo acknowledgement and sign-in session. The application source does not include advertising or analytics cookies. The application loads Google Fonts and Bootstrap resources from jsDelivr; those providers receive requests from your browser, including technical connection information. Their own policies apply to their services. You can clear the session cookie in your browser, which ends the remembered session and acknowledgement.</p><h2>Storage and requests</h2><p>Entries and accounts remain in the database until they are removed; no automatic retention period is configured in the application source. Contact Aziz at the address above to ask about access, correction or deletion. Hosting and database providers may retain operational logs or backups under their own settings and policies.</p><p>Last updated: 5 November 2026</p></main></body></html>
